  "explain_en": "Bari tori (deburring) is the work of smoothing sharp edges after cutting a pipe. Tools such as a dedicated reamer or a scraper are used for this work. However, Kantan Boushoku Tsugite (pipe-end anti-corrosion joint) is an installation component, not a tool for grinding or removing burrs.\n\nVocabulary:\n取(と)り作業(さぎょう): Removal work / Taking off\n使用(しよう): Use\n工具(こうぐ): Tool\n管用(かんよう): For pipes\n管端(かんたん)防食(ぼうしょく)継手(つぎて): Pipe-end anti-corrosion joint\nねじ切(き)り機(き): Threading machine",
